<title>JAPAN: Hirabo bid-only after third-party allotment news.</title>
<headline>Hirabo bid-only after third-party allotment news.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in fishing nets maker Hirabo Corp were bid-only on the Tokyo Stock Exchange on Tuesday morning after the company announced that it planned a third-party allotment of 7.12 million new shares.  </p>
<p>By 0045 GMT, Hirabo was bid-only at 320 yen. It ended at 300 yen on Monday.</p>
<p>Hirabo said on Monday that it would issue 7.12 million new shares worth 2.5 billion yen to two unlisted firms belonging to the Chisan group on March 13, with the aim of strengthening its financial condition.</p>
